<DocsLayout
  slug="faq"
  title="FAQ & troubleshooting"
  description="Common signing errors, and how to get unstuck."
>
  <h2 id="no-signing-certificate-found">"No signing certificate 'iOS Distribution' found"</h2>
  <p>
    Your Apple Distribution certificate hasn't been uploaded to this project's Vault yet, or was
    uploaded to a different project. Check the Secrets screen and re-upload if needed — see <a
      href="/docs/ios-signing">iOS signing</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="provisioning-profile-expired">Provisioning profile expired</h2>
  <p>
    Apple provisioning profiles carry a fixed expiry date. Generate a new one from your Apple
    Developer account and upload it to the Vault — pkgr.app doesn't auto-renew certificates or
    profiles on your behalf today.
  </p>

  <h2 id="i-lost-my-android-keystore">I lost my Android keystore</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/docs/android-signing#if-you-lose-your-keystore">Android signing</a> — pkgr.app can't
    recover a keystore it was never given a backup of.
  </p>

  <h2 id="a-build-seems-stuck-in-queued">A build seems stuck in "queued"</h2>
  <p>
    Check GitHub Actions directly for the repository. pkgr.app triggers the run, but the actual
    queue is GitHub's own runner capacity — not something pkgr.app controls.
  </p>

  <h2 id="my-staging-install-link-disappeared">My staging install link disappeared</h2>
  <p>
    Staging artifacts expire on a plan-based schedule — see <a href="/docs/ota-installs#artifact-retention"
      >artifact retention</a
    >. Trigger a new build to get a fresh, installable one.
  </p>

  <h2 id="still-stuck">Still stuck?</h2>
  <p>
    Check <a href="/status">status</a> for ongoing incidents, or <a href="/contact">reach out</a> directly.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
